Hello List,

my name is Max, I'm editor at Linux New Media, publisher of
Linux-Magazin (German) and Linux-Magazine (English) beneath others.

I received that e-mail about a new product called UMLMON. It is an
addition to UML for monitoring one or more instances of UML. See
http://www.gerd-stolpmann.de/buero/umlmon.html for details. It is not
open source I think.

My question to you is: Do you know that piece of software? Is it a
worthy product? Is there other software which does more or less the
same (perhaps even open source software)?

What do you think of UMLMON?

